  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Owen, you're verified. I found the order. It was delivered within the last 48 hours, and nothing was auto-refunded for the pho. One beef pho is $15.00, and you have two ways to be compensated:\n\n1. **Refund to your Visa ending 4242:** $12.00. This is the $15.00 pho minus its $3.00 share of your WELCOME10 promo discount. That $3.00 share is added to your account as credit. You'd get $12.00 on your card and $3.00 in credit.\n2. **Account credit only:** $18.00, which is the pho's price plus 20%, for future orders.\n\nWhich would you like?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hmm, I'd really rather have the money back on my card, not credit. I don't think $12 is right though. I'm not sure what I paid for the pho after the promo, but I want the full amount I actually paid for that missing pho back on my card. Can you check what I was charged for it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked, and the $12.00 is correct.\n\nYour order subtotal was $50.00, and WELCOME10 took $10.00 off. That's 20% of the subtotal, so each item's price is discounted by 20%. For the missing pho:\n\n- Price: $15.00\n- Its share of the discount: $10.00 \u00d7 15 \u00f7 50 = $3.00\n- What you effectively paid for it: **$12.00**\n\nUnder our policy, the card refund is $12.00. The $3.00 discount share can't go back to the card and is issued as account credit instead. So your total is $15.00 in value: $12.00 on your card and $3.00 in credit.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead with the $12.00 card refund and the $3.00 credit?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I see the math. I was hoping for the full $15 on my card, but I get that the promo was taken out across the order. I'd like the $12 on my card and the $3 credit, please."
  },
